data: {"type":"turn.done","id":"01m192zfhdcsmqxd39bdf097w6","created_at":"2026-08-30T10:20:55.725Z","state":{"status":"done","output":{"content":"**`rollbackVerified: true`** with empty `rollbackResidue`. The simulation succeeded. Now I have everything needed for the blast-radius report. Let me also capture the exact operation/rollback SQL to a file for reference.\n\n---\n\n## Blast-Radius Report — DELETE payments of inactive customers\n\n**Simulation id:** `d777e8a9`\n**Database:** `pagila` (production)\n**Definition used:** `customer.active = 0` (the Pagila inactive flag — 15 customers)\n\n### What will be destroyed\n\n| Table | Before | After | Rows deleted |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `public.payment` | 16,049 | 15,644 | **405** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_01` | 1,157 | 1,123 | **34** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_02` | 2,312 | 2,251 | **61** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_03` | 5,644 | 5,524 | **120** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_04` | 6,754 | 6,568 | **186** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_05` | 182 | 178 | **4** |\n| `public.payment_p2020_06` | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| **Total** | | | **810 rows** |\n\nNo other tables touched. All payment-table FKs are `NO ACTION` so no cascade damage to `rental`, `staff`, or `customer`.\n\n### Proof of reversibility\n\n`rollbackVerified: true`, `rollbackResidue: []` — the rollback was executed in the sandbox clone, every table checksum returned to its pre-operation value, and no backup residue remains.\n\n### Exact operation SQL\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment              AS SELECT * FROM payment;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_01     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_01;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_02     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_02;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_03     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_03;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_04     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_04;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_05     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_05;\nCREATE TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_06     AS SELECT * FROM payment_p2020_06;\n\nDELETE FROM payment              p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_01     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_02     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_03     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_04     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_05     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\nDELETE FROM payment_p2020_06     p USING customer c WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND c.active = 0;\n```\n\n### Exact rollback SQL (verified, kept on file)\n\n```sql\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment;\nINSERT INTO payment              SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_01;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_01     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_01;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_02;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_02     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_02;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_03;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_03     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_03;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_04;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_04     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_04;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_05;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_05     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_05;\nTRUNCATE TABLE payment_p2020_06;\nINSERT INTO payment_p2020_06     SELECT * FROM saferun_bak_payment_p2020_06;\n\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_01;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_02;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_03;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_04;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_05;\nDROP TABLE saferun_bak_payment_p2020_06;\n```\n\n### ⚠️ One caveat worth knowing before you approve\n\nThese rows are **financial records** (16,049 payments is the full payment history). Even though the customers are flagged inactive, deleting payment history is usually something accounting/finance wants a say on, not just marketing. If \"marketing wants cleaner analytics\" is the actual driver, a safer alternative is to mark them excluded in the analytics layer (a view, a column, a flag) rather than physically delete from the source of truth.\n\n---\n\n**I am stopped.** I will not touch production until you give explicit approval. Reply with \"yes\" (or the equivalent) to execute simulation `d777e8a9` against the production database. If you want me to redesign — e.g. exclude payments older than a retention floor, or stop here and just produce a soft-delete view instead — say the word.","type":"model.message","id":"01m192z5mqwhvezqw0j5108mp1","created_at":"2026-08-30T10:20:55.720Z","thread_id":"main","finish_reason":"stop","usage":{"input_tokens":18374,"output_tokens":1236,"cache_read_tokens":15469,"input_tokens_breakdown":{"harness":3566,"skills":191,"instructions":167,"tool_definitions":0,"messages":14450}}},"required_actions":[],"completed_at":"2026-08-30T10:20:55.725Z","metrics":{"total_input_tokens":68901,"total_output_tokens":4506,"total_tokens":73407,"total_cache_read_tokens":60243,"total_reasoning_tokens":0}},"thread_id":null}
